 "wt-doc-capture": {
  "technical": "wt_doc_capture",
  "name": "WT Document Capture: Scanner & Hot Folder to Odoo",
  "summary": "Scan paper and pick up copier folders straight into Odoo with a free Windows agent: WIA scanners with feeder and duplex, hot folders, separator sheets and QR labels, local OCR in English and Arabic, a document inbox and edit in place with versions.",
  "intro": [
   "Paper still arrives every day: bills, delivery notes, signed contracts, ID copies. Scanners and the copier's scan-to-folder share are local to the office, so a browser cannot drive them. The free WT Document Capture agent for Windows can, and this module is where its documents land."
  ],
  "sections": [
   {
    "heading": "Why a Windows agent",
    "bullets": [
     "Scan from any WIA scanner: flatbed or document feeder, both sides, resolution and colour, straight into one multi-page PDF.",
     "Hot folders on the PC or on a network share (for example the copier's scan folder). Each folder has a routing rule, and the file is moved to a \"processed\" folder or deleted afterwards.",
     "Separator sheets and QR labels printed from Odoo split a stack of pages into documents and send each part to its record. Scan twenty delivery notes in one go.",
     "Local OCR with Tesseract, English and Arabic included. The PDF becomes searchable and the agent reads the reference number, the VAT number and the total.",
     "Vendor bill drafts with the vendor found by VAT number, the bill reference, the date and the total, and the PDF attached to the bill.",
     "Edit in place: open an Odoo attachment in its Windows program, save, and it comes back as a new version on the same record. Older versions are kept.",
     "Drag and drop files and Outlook e-mails (.msg and .eml) onto the agent window.",
     "Offline queue: if the internet drops, documents wait on the PC and go up when it is back. Large files resume where they stopped."
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "Where documents go",
    "bullets": [
     "Document Inbox: someone files it later.",
     "Attach by reference: the reference or a barcode on the page (PO00042, S00017, a bill number, a customer reference) finds the record, and the PDF is attached and posted in its chatter.",
     "Vendor bill draft: installed automatically with Invoicing.",
     "Documents app: when the Odoo Enterprise Documents module is installed."
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "Set up in 4 steps",
    "bullets": [
     "Install the agent on the PC with the scanner. The download link is on the setup checklist in Odoo.",
     "Pair it: in Odoo, Document Capture, Configuration, Agents, create an agent and click \"Generate pairing code\". Open the invite link on the PC. Nobody types tokens or addresses.",
     "Devices found: the agent's setup wizard lists the scanners on the PC and lets you add hot folders. Odoo shows what it found.",
     "First document received: scan a page or drop a PDF in a hot folder. Each step gets a green tick."
    ]
   },
   {
    "heading": "Security",
    "bullets": [
     "Pairing codes work once, for 24 hours. Odoo stores only a hash of the agent token; the PC keeps the token encrypted with Windows DPAPI.",
     "The agent works as one Odoo user with that user's rights. Users, groups, settings and technical models can never be the target of a scan.",
     "An agent can be revoked at any time from Odoo."
    ]
   }
  ],
  "category": "Productivity/Documents",
  "suite": "Hardware and Desktop Apps",
  "version": "19.0.1.0.0",
  "versions": [
   "19.0",
   "20.0"
  ],
  "latestVersion": "20.0.1.0.0",
  "price": 129.0,
  "currency": "USD",
  "storeUrl": "https://apps.odoo.com/apps/modules/19.0/wt_doc_capture/",
  "storeUrls": {
   "19.0": "https://apps.odoo.com/apps/modules/19.0/wt_doc_capture/",
   "20.0": "https://apps.odoo.com/apps/modules/20.0/wt_doc_capture/"
  },
  "published": true
 },
